<!--Post: 2059--><!--Time: 1103271745-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2059"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->About &#34;Christ On The Cross&#34;s&#39; &#40;BTK?&#41; post. He says: <BR> <BR>&#34;TO address the connection between myself and op. &#34;Barn door&#34;, I would say that this is false.&#34; <BR> <BR>Anyone know what the heck he&#39;s referring to??<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2059-->
<!--Post: 2060--><!--Time: 1103276047-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2060"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->C<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 1:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#62; The ZKC is KANSAS CITY &#40;ARTCC&#41;,KS. Which is in OLathe KS.  <BR>&#62; The K50 is COOK AIRFIELD INC. In Derby which is 2 minutes out of Wichita proper.  <BR>&#62; Are there photos stashed at these locations?  <BR> <BR>When I said stashed - I was thinking in terms of looking for a white plastic bag around or about these locations. Given the recent park find, if it turns out to be authentic, it seems plausible someone is trying point to more &#34;packages&#34;. <BR> <BR>Interesting that ARTCC stands for Air Route Traffic Control Center - wonder if he learned to speak that way as an air traffic controller or pilot? <BR> <BR>Mea Culpa for posting my decryption in an inappropriate thread... <BR> <BR>- C<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2060-->
<!--Post: 2061--><!--Time: 1103277018-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2061"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:thekingbeatsoff@histrailer.lots" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lightbringer<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 1:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have not been able to find satisfactory info on op. barn door either, victor. could it have been a secret operation, or perhaps something he coined himself?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2061-->
<!--Post: 2062--><!--Time: 1103278357-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2062"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->man<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 2:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->no op barn door is a method police use to validate a search<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2062-->
<!--Post: 2065--><!--Time: 1103284912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2065"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->PokingAround<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 4:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I took China&#39;s work to mean that the baby photo sent in April was presaged by the code on the letter in March.  The photo looks like a one year old.  50 means 1950, making BTK&#39;s birth year 1949 instead of 39.  And yes, KCK could refer to Kansas City, Kansas.  Sorry if this has already been mentioned.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2065-->
<!--Post: 2066--><!--Time: 1103286128-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2066"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->PokingAround<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 4:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->P.S. A birth year of 1949 better matches the age in the witnesses&#39;s descriptions of BTK.   <BR> <BR>In answer to speculation on the other thread, I&#39;ve never heard that Otero worked at Cook.  Did he?  I thought he worked at Jabara or thereabouts.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2066-->
<!--Post: 2068--><!--Time: 1103289716-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2068"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 5:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe in these places ZKC and K50 there´s a panel or a employees book &#40;i dont know how do you call it in the US&#41; with BTK´s picture.  <BR>I think he might worked in these places.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2068-->
<!--Post: 2069--><!--Time: 1103291112-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2069"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->PokingAround<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 5:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay, just read the 1974 Eagle article again and Otero definitely worked at Cook, near Rose Hill.  Also said that he attained the rank of technical sergeant while in the service. <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2069-->
<!--Post: 2070--><!--Time: 1103291188-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2070"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->China<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 5:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why did my ASCII post get deleted?  I&#39;m sorry it was in the wrong spot, but I was right, wasn&#39;t I??<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2070-->
<!--Post: 2072--><!--Time: 1103291827-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2072"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Electraqtkitty<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 5:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I somehow doubt that the people/person who was posting messages on the &#34;from BTK&#34; board was actually him. I agree with the profile on the website that he probably is web savvy, because it&#39;s yet another source of information to read about himself, and his impact on society. But why would he post? I&#39;m thinking he would know that his post could help trace him.  <BR> <BR>Or am I wrong in thinking that he could be traced? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2072-->
<!--Post: 2075--><!--Time: 1103295310-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2075"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 6:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->CHINA wrote: &#34;Why did my ASCII post get deleted? I&#39;m sorry it was in the wrong spot, but I was right, wasn&#39;t I??&#34; <BR> <BR>I can&#39;t say for sure, but I also had a nice post in that same &#34;MESSAGES to BTK&#34; deleted. Tom said it was because it didn&#39;t fit that thread. THAT&#39;S WHY I STARTED THIS THREAD. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know ASCII code, but it looks like you may have been the 1st to crack the person claiming to be BTKs&#39; code &#40;on the &#34;MESAGES from BTK&#34; thread&#41; yesterday, Dec 16! GREAT WORK! Let&#39;s see what more comes of it.    Victor<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2075-->
<!--Post: 2076--><!--Time: 1103295396-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2076"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 6:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s a thought...   If you hover on the &#34;Christ on the Cross&#34; moniker, you will see the mailto address as being <a href="mailto:beattheking@neverwill.ever">beattheking@neverwill.ever</a> on his/her message dated 12/09/04. The only other moniker that shows a similar mailto address is &#34;Lightbringer&#34;; showing a mailto address of <a href="mailto:kingbeaten@oneday.soon">kingbeaten@oneday.soon</a> on his/her message dated 12/15/04 and a mailto address of <a href="mailto:thekingbeatsoff@histrailor.lots">thekingbeatsoff@histrailor.lots</a> on his/her message dated 12/17/04.  Perhaps someone is just having some fun, but it is quite a coincidence as common sense tells us that neverwill.ever, oneday.soon, and histrailor.lots are NOT valid domain names.   <BR> <BR>Anyone? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2076-->
<!--Post: 2077--><!--Time: 1103295422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2077"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->hta<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 6:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I posted the same decryption a day after it showed up in the &#34;Messages from BTK&#34; thread and it was deleted.  Seems now everyone is paying attention to it now that it&#39;s been brought up 5 or so times.  A bit discouraging to those of us who are participating without a userid on this board. <BR> <BR>This thread is a good idea... <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2077-->
<!--Post: 2078--><!--Time: 1103295633-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2078"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->China<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 7:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I figured someone should have got that sooner as ASCII is a pretty common thing among people that know about computers.  Good job, hta!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2078-->
<!--Post: 2081--><!--Time: 1103302280-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2081"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->C<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 8:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->FWIW, yesterday when I associated ZKC K50 with the ICAO locations codes I searched to see if someone had already figured that out before my December 16, 2004 - 6:39 pm post in &#34;Messages to BTK, Part 2&#34; - there was no mention of it. <BR> <BR>Posting plain ASCII is so childishly obvious it did cross my mind that this is the work of a younger reader with a warped sense of humor. However, the K50 -&#62; cook airfield reference is too intriguing to be ignored. <BR> <BR>- C <BR> <BR>BTW, I am not the same poster as China<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2081-->
<!--Post: 2083--><!--Time: 1103303654-->
