<!--Post: 2086--><!--Time: 1103308423-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2086"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Somerset<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 10:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I disagree, the person posting is saying that we should look at them in groups of 6, hence the ellipses. Which lead me to this: <BR> <BR><b>I believe these are colors for the following reasons :</b> <BR>All colors can be made up of the combination of 6 numbers and letters. These numbers are 0-9 but the letters are A-F only. The last post in the &#34;From:” forum was a clue and a direction, not a reiteration. <BR> <BR>I was thinking a high-school or a college color palette? I checked the high-schools and they seem to have only colors which are more saturated. So if in fact these are colors, if poses the question,  <BR>&#34;A corporate color palette or an educational one?&#34; <BR> <BR>All of the colors are very similar and I believe that is more than a random occurrence. The last color, however, makes no sense to me. <BR> <BR>So maybe they signify victim’s names, streets or something along those lines? Green Ave. Mr. Brown  or things like that.  <BR> <BR>I tried posting the table with the colors, but the filter stopped it and stripped out the attributes in the tags. <BR> <BR>I will be checking the board later, if there is someone way I can work around the filter to show the colors please leave a post and I will post the full colored table cell version. The &#34;Enable HTML button&#34; is checked, fyi. <BR> <BR>So for now, if you were to copy and paste the code into a .txt file then rename the extension to .htm, then drag it into your browser you would see what I&#39;m talking about. <BR> <BR> <BR>&#60;table&#62; <BR>  &#60;tr&#62; <BR>    &#60;td&#62;&#60;font face=&#34;Arial,&#34; color=&#34;#5A4B43&#34; size=&#34;2&#34;&#62;<b>5A4B43</b>&#60;/font&#62;&#60;/td&#62; <BR>    &#60;td&#62;&#60;font face=&#34;Arial,&#34; color=&#34;#4B3530&#34; size=&#34;2&#34;&#62;<b>4B3530</b>&#60;/font&#62;&#60;/td&#62; <BR>    &#60;td&#62;&#60;font face=&#34;Arial,&#34; color=&#34;#70686F&#34; size=&#34;2&#34;&#62;<b>70686F</b>&#60;/font&#62;&#60;/td&#62; <BR>    &#60;td&#62;&#60;font face=&#34;Arial,&#34; color=&#34;#746F42&#34; size=&#34;2&#34;&#62;<b>746F42</b>&#60;/font&#62;&#60;/td&#62; <BR>	&#60;td&#62;&#60;font face=&#34;Arial,&#34; color=&#34;#544B&#34; size=&#34;2&#34;&#62;<b>544B</b>??&#60;/font&#62;&#60;/td&#62; <BR>  &#60;/tr&#62; <BR>&#60;/table&#62;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2086-->
<!--Post: 2088--><!--Time: 1103309108-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2088"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pondering<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 10:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Internet cafes, libraries, any business he may stop and do IT repair work in that day, even motels and hotels have accessible computers now.  Sending from a different IP each day &#40;even at the same time&#41; is not that hard once you think about it. <BR> <BR>Like Kelleher said, BTK is not only computer savvy, but electronics savvy.  Radio operations are right up his alley and may have been what connected him to Otero at Cook.  This last code seems to ask us to look harder at that.  And thinking about it, there had to have been something of an incendiary nature pass between them &#40;Otero and BTK&#41; at some point.  In one of his letters to the police BTK said &#34;You guess the motive!&#34; A taunt which would have any Sherlock worth his Holmes looking hard at Otero to find out what was going on in his life past and present. <BR> <BR>BTK&#39;s period of inactivity after mid-80&#39;s may have been due to a combination of factors, chief among them the accessibility of the proliferation of bizarre, grotesque sites on the internet where any fetish can be fulfilled and any fetishist with the right equipment can bring it all right into his own living space &#40;including simulated asphyxiations.&#41;  <BR> <BR>And don&#39;t forget the advent of Oprah and Jerry Springer, where every nature of being encased in flesh came into our living rooms to air their sicknesses and make what was once freakish and abnormal seem entirely mundane. <BR> <BR>I do believe BTK has a naughty secret.  Something that&#39;s shamed him from an early age.  Perhaps it&#39;s this that gnaws at him and provides impetus for the creation of these cryptic puzzles and games that draw attention away from anything but what his intelligence quotient might be.  He doesn&#39;t want us looking at anything else.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2088-->
<!--Post: 2091--><!--Time: 1103309893-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2091"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 10:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Otero was ,more than likely a personal grudge. He went out after the whole family. If he could have got them all, he probably would have. Something I find intresting is the fact that Otero&#39;s surviving son gets out of pison in December, and BTK resurfaces. He might have it out for this bloodline, like in Last of the Mohikans? Cant spell sorry. The question that still gets me is, was the Otero family really the first killings. <BR>Also I was a 31V in the Army and that is a communications job. Like alot of ex military, I work for a military contractor. Lots of travel, especially in comms. Maybe he is a &#34;hometown killer&#34; but maybe he doesn&#39;t live at home anymore. What yall think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2091-->
<!--Post: 2092--><!--Time: 1103310978-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2092"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Good Cop<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 11:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey hmmm, your right on the mark about time of day. Maybe he just sits down in the lobby of a building with his laptop and casually uses their wire-less connection. &#40;The courts have ruled that this is not illegal by the way. As long as you don&#39;t pretend to be with that company&#41; <BR> <BR>My 14 year old nephew and his friends ride around on their skateboards all the time. When they get tired and take a break, they sit outside a business, take their laptops out of their backpack and and go at it. He even uses it to place phone calls to my sister to let her know where he and his friends are at. He has this little head set thing that plugs into the laptop. Great kid, my sister never has to worry about him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2092-->
<!--Post: 2093--><!--Time: 1103311352-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2093"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that its strange that a 60 someodd year old man can go to public places and use the internet and not be some how strange. Maybe the authoities need to keep a look out for this. Like you said, Good cop, the laptop thing is an easy way to make contact. So if anyone sees a 60 someodd man with a laptop aound 5 pm, the flags should go up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2093-->
<!--Post: 2095--><!--Time: 1103311484-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2095"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Probablystretching<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 11:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Somerset, is one of the colors gold?  There&#39;s a Golden limo service near Lewis and Mosley.  Lewis street also intersects with Green street and Greenwood street, which is super close to Hydraulic, where one of BTK&#39;s victim&#39;s lived. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2095-->
<!--Post: 2096--><!--Time: 1103311527-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2096"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 11:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Or if the authoities should check all public access computers for related webpages. He likes the libray and public places to make his statements. Thee is a way to find him if hes using public resorces.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2096-->
