<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2098"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Somerset<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 11:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And not only is the last color is gold, but it is green based on how your browser fills in the missing two colors. If its done in photoshop, its green.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
