<!--Post: 2100--><!--Time: 1103312101-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2100"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stretchingfurther<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Somerset, look at the beginning letters in the message from TedCammon.  Unscrambling some of the letters you can make &#39;boys gym&#39;.  Made me think of Truesdell Jr. High, in the &#34;South&#34; part of the city, school colors green and gold.  Not saying this means anything, but it&#39;s weird how you can suddenly start making things fit into something bizarre.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2100-->
<!--Post: 2102--><!--Time: 1103313923-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2102"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mills<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know this may have nothing to do with anything but when I look at those colors, I noticed that they look like the colors you get from a polaroid. The colors that dark/ black skin develop as in polaroids. I&#39;ve had a lot of experience working with polaroids in the past and this was the first thing that stuck out when I saw those colors. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2102-->
