<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2103"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pondering<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;The colors that dark/ black skin develop as in polaroids.&#34; <BR> <BR>Can you clarify?  You mean before the photo is processing, during, or after?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2103-->
<!--Post: 2104--><!--Time: 1103314363-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2104"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Somerset<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What if he is not white? And those are skin tones and blonde hair?  <BR> <BR>&#34;Someone who inherits hemoglobin S from one parent and normal hemoglobin &#40;A&#41; from the other parent will have sickle cell trait. Approximately 8% of African Americans have sickle cell trait.&#34; <BR> <BR>Would come close to matching that 6% as earlier stated.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2104-->
<!--Post: 2105--><!--Time: 1103314922-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2105"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I dont know. I think the &#34;code&#34; is a fake. Come on, its too impersonal. You cant forget, this guy is 60 plus. He may be computer saavy and all that, but the code is too much. Not his style. He&#39;s a copycat type of guy. Hes been at this fo years. He may possably be reading this and may be writing some of these posts. Hes a clever guy and a simple color code is just not him. He wont be giving us &#34;nomal&#34; folks any hints. Hes out to mess with the cops, and to scare us. A question to Tom, What posts do you think may really be his?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2105-->
<!--Post: 2106--><!--Time: 1103315044-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2106"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pondering<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I may be wrong, but I believe the 6% has to do with his non-secretor status, Somerset.  There is one variation found in only 6% of Caucasians.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2106-->
<!--Post: 2107--><!--Time: 1103316012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2107"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->C<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Somerset, Sorry, but the statistical probability that the color hex values would work out to be ASCII characters that just happened to be ICAO locations for Cook Airfield, KS ARTCC, and the word &#34;photo&#34;, then signed &#34;BTK&#34;  is astronomical to say the least. I think you&#39;re way off on this. There is no color code.  It is clear: <BR> <BR>5A4B43 = ZKC <BR>4B3530 = K50 <BR>70686F 746F = photo <BR>42544B = BTK <BR> <BR>The only mystery here is whether this came from some poser clown - or the real btk... <BR> <BR>- C<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2107-->
<!--Post: 2108--><!--Time: 1103316454-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2108"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 12:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m with &#34;C&#34; above. <BR> <BR>Victor<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2108-->
<!--Post: 2112--><!--Time: 1103318104-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2112"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Somerset<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 1:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Astronomical like the fact that no one on Earth has yet to crack Zodiac&#39;s puzzle? <BR> <BR>Or astronomical in the way that serial killers don&#39;t lie dormant for a decade or two? <BR> <BR>Or the same type probability that the colors are all in the same family, only minor shade differences between them? <BR> <BR>Or did you mean that it was the same type of probability that the police have a fingerprint, DNA, semen, and correspondences yet still have no killer 30 years later? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m saying that given the subject matter here, nothing should be ruled out. I love the solution he posted this morning, but that doesn&#39;t mean we can&#39;t continue to look at other possibilities and meanings. Those are the same close-minded attitudes that have kept this case open for 30 years. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2112-->
<!--Post: 2113--><!--Time: 1103318183-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2113"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->wade<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 1:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah....its not color.  I have spent alot of time checking out the various ARTCC codes and there is no way it is&#39;nt about the airports. <BR>What are the chances??  Then the last two words are &#34;btk photo&#34;....that probability probably barely exist even in any hypothetical mathematical equation.  Along with C, it is either btk or some other loser posted it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2113-->
