<!--Post: 2126--><!--Time: 1103326379-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2126"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 3:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Somerset was on to something when &#40;s&#41;he translated the 5A4B43 post into color codes, but to elaborate: the content of this post is a hexadecimal string. <BR> <BR>That&#39;s undoubtedly Greek to some of you. In a nutshell, hex is a base-16 numeric system mostly used in PC computing. You have the normal 0-9, and then A=10, B=11, C=12, etc. You can convert hex numbers into decimal using any of the many <a href="http://www.mrcalculator.com/hexdec.html">hexadecimal calculators</a> available on the web. <BR> <BR>Anyhoo... <BR> <BR>This post allegedly from BTK, translated into decimal, comes to 1.8313798029334936e&#43;33. Does that number or sequence of numbers mean anything significant to anyone? <BR> <BR>Taking them in chunks: <BR> <BR>5A4B43 = 5917507 <BR>4B3530 = 4928816 <BR>70686F = 7366767 <BR>746F42 = 7630658 <BR>544B = 21579 <BR> <BR>Any ideas?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2126-->
